[center][size=6][b][color=#ffff00]Simple Time-lapse[/color][/b][/size]
[size=1]Time-lapse, Timelapse, Time Lapse? Nobody knows![/size]
[i]Create stunning time-lapse scenes of Night City with a single button press.[/i]

[size=4][b]Check out the Videos tab for examples![/b][/size][/center]
[line]
[size=3]Simple Time-lapse gives you control over the flow of time in Night City.

It handles the setup for cinematic recording: hiding the HUD, holding your position, silencing the radio and notifications, and then putting everything back exactly as it was when you are done.[/size]

[color=#ffff00][b]Updating from v1.3.0 - read this first[/b][/color]
[list]
[*][b]Two new requirements.[/b] The window is rebuilt on [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/26589]Window Utils[/url], and hiding the HUD now goes through [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/7780]Codeware[/url]. Install both before updating. Without Window Utils the window will not draw, though your hotkeys still work.[/*]
[*][b]Unlock Speed Limit is gone.[/b] The engine caps simulation at 10x whatever it is told, so the setting never did anything. Simulation Mode now goes to 10x and stops there.[/*]
[*][b]Jump to Time is now Set Time on Start[/b], and it has a companion: Restore Time on Stop puts the clock back where it was.[/*]
[*][b]Your settings carry over.[/b] Anything new arrives at its default.[/*]
[/list]

[color=#ffff00][b]New in v2.0.0[/b][/color]
[list]
[*][b]A rebuilt window[/b] with tabs, a pinned summary of what the run will do, and the clock and START always in reach.[/*]
[*][b]Presets.[/b] Defaults, Sunrise, City Rush and Empty City ship with the mod, and you can save your own.[/*]
[*][b]A Cinema section[/b] - a moving camera, depth of field, camera shake, a weather sequence, cinematic bars and fades. Needs [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/30296]XUtils[/url], and the rest of the mod works without it.[/*]
[*][b]Auto Speed for Clock Mode.[/b] Give it a start time, an end time, how many days to cross and how long the run lasts, and it works the speed out for you.[/*]
[*][b]Audio control.[/b] Mute the radio, the score, sound effects and notifications for the length of a run. A call that arrives mid-run has its ringtone cut.[/*]
[*][b]Clock Mode reaches three game hours per real second.[/b][/*]
[/list]
[line]
[size=5][b][color=#ffff00]Features[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Two Time-lapse Modes:[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Simulation Mode:[/b] Speeds up everything, to the engine's limit of 10x. Best for busy intersections and flowing traffic.[/*]
[*][b]Clock Mode:[/b] Speeds up only the sky and lighting, up to three game hours per real second. Best for atmospheric transition shots.[/*]
[/list][/*]
[*][b]Presets:[/b] A named recipe carries every setting but the log level. Four ship with the mod, and saving your own takes one button.[/*]
[*][b]Run Summary:[/b] Mode, speed, length and start time in one line above the panel, with an icon for every option the run will apply.[/*]
[*][b]Smart HUD Control:[/b] Hides the whole HUD for the run, the vehicle HUD included, and restores it afterwards. Other mods' on-screen overlays are left alone.[/*]
[*][b]Steady Camera:[/b] Holds movement, weapons and camera rotation for a tripod shot, and turns off head bob.[/*]
[*][b]Audio Control:[/b] Mute the radio, the score, sound effects and notifications for the run. Each one comes back on Stop.[/*]
[*][b]Scene Control:[/b]
[list]
[*]Disable flying AVs for clean skylines.[/*]
[*]Disable crowds and street traffic for an empty city.[/*]
[*]Traffic Frenzy speeds up nearby vehicles, with an adjustable multiplier.[/*]
[/list][/*]
[*][b]Precision Control:[/b]
[list]
[*]Ctrl+click any slider to type an exact value.[/*]
[*]Set a duration or run until you stop it.[/*]
[*]Set Time on Start skips straight to golden hour, and Restore Time on Stop puts the clock back.[/*]
[/list][/*]
[*][b]Safety:[/b]
[list]
[*]Refuses to start while you are in combat, which you can turn off.[/*]
[*]Stops the run when you open the pause or hub menus, and says so when you return.[/*]
[*]Clamps the speed when switching modes so physics does not explode.[/*]
[*]Every change a run makes is put back on Stop, and panic buttons on the Debug tab cover anything a crash left behind.[/*]
[/list][/*]
[/list]
[line]
[size=5][b][color=#ffff00]Cinema - with XUtils installed[/color][/b][/size]

Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/30296]XUtils[/url] by CyanideX and the Cinema tab fills in. Without it the tab says so and nothing else changes.

[list]
[*][b]Camera:[/b] Static holds the frame where the run started. Free fly moves the camera on WASD, Space and C at a speed you set, and brings V along so the city keeps loading around the shot. V is hidden either way.[/*]
[*][b]Free fly controls:[/b] Q and E roll, the wheel sets speed, Ctrl is precision, and holding R, F or X with the wheel sets roll, field of view or look sensitivity. These are your own XUtils bindings, so rebinding them under XUtils in Mod Settings works here too.[/*]
[*][b]Camera Shake:[/b] The recipes XUtils ships - handheld, sway, subtle, cinematic and more - over a static camera, with a strength slider.[/*]
[*][b]Depth of Field:[/b] A real lens on the camera, with five named presets from Natural to Dreamy, autofocus, and full control of focal length, aperture and blur.[/*]
[*][b]Weather Sequence:[/b] Move through a list of weather states across the run, split evenly, by percentage, or by game hours each. The natural weather returns on Stop.[/*]
[*][b]Framing:[/b] Cinematic bars at 2.39:1, 2.00:1 or 1.85:1, and a fade in at the start or out at the end.[/*]
[/list]
[line]
[size=5][b][color=#ffff00]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/107]Cyber Engine Tweaks[/url][/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/26589]Window Utils[/url] - the mod window is drawn with it[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/7780]Codeware[/url] - hiding the HUD needs it[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/30296]XUtils[/url] - optional, for the Cinema section[/*]
[/list]
[line]
[size=5][b][color=#ffff00]How to Use[/color][/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Open the [b]Cyber Engine Tweaks[/b] overlay.[/*]
[*]Bind a hotkey for [b]"Start/Stop Time-lapse"[/b].[/*]
[*](Optional) Bind a hotkey for [b]"Toggle HUD"[/b] for quick screenshots.[/*]
[*]Pick a preset, or set the mode, speed and duration yourself.[/*]
[*]Close the overlay, frame your shot, and hit the hotkey.[/*]
[/list][center][youtube]DklQ6SAhm10[/youtube][/center]
[line]
[size=5][b][color=#ffff00]Compatibility[/color][/b][/size]

Works with:
[list]
[*][b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/12369]Balanced Nighttime Cycle[/url][/b] (Respects new cycle timings)[/*]
[*][b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/18027]Weather Switcher[/url][/b] (Great for locking weather before a shot)[/*]
[*][b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/12490]Nova City 2[/url][/b][/*]
[/list]
[line]
[size=5][b][color=#ffff00]Known issues[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Vehicles are hard-coded to ignore time dilation in the physics engine. In Simulation Mode nearby vehicles run at normal speed unless Traffic Frenzy is on.[/*]
[*]Traffic Frenzy is experimental. Cars may corner aggressively, briefly stop, or behave unusually at higher multipliers.[/*]
[*]Camera Shake applies to a static camera. A free fly camera is driven by XUtils every frame, so a shake laid over it would not survive the frame.[/*]
[*]Simulation Mode cannot exceed 10x. The engine caps it there whatever it is asked for.[/*]
[/list]
[line]
[size=5][b][color=#ffff00]Installation[/color][/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/107]Cyber Engine Tweaks[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/26589]Window Utils[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/7780]Codeware[/url].[/*]
[*]Download and install with a mod manager, or[/*]
[*]Download and extract the zip file.[/*]
[*]Drop the [b]bin[/b] folder into your Cyberpunk 2077 directory.
[font=Courier New]Cyberpunk 2077\bin\x64\plugins\cyber_engine_tweaks\mods\simple_timelapse\[/font][/*]
[/list]
